# MyAcs — Local Network Screen Mirroring Application

I want to develop a powerful, reliable, and user-friendly screen mirroring application named **MyAcs** that works entirely over a local area network (LAN), without requiring an internet connection.

### Core Requirements

1. **Permanent Device ID:** When I install MyAcs on a PC, the application should automatically generate a unique, permanent device ID that remains the same even after restarting the PC or closing the application.

2. **Screen Mirroring:** I should be able to install MyAcs on another PC, enter the target PC's device ID, and instantly view its screen over the local network.

3. **View-Only Access:** The application must support screen viewing only. It must not include remote mouse control, keyboard input, file transfer, or any other remote-control functionality.

4. **Background Operation:** After installation and initial setup, MyAcs should run as a background service. Closing the application window must not stop screen mirroring or disable access to the PC.

5. **Automatic Startup:** MyAcs should automatically start when Windows boots and continue running in the background, even after the user closes the application window or restarts the computer.

6. **Persistent Device Availability:** The target PC should remain available for screen mirroring whenever it is powered on and connected to the local network, without requiring the user to open the application manually each time.

7. **Local Network Only:** All screen streaming and device communication must remain within the local network. The application must not depend on cloud servers, external relays, or internet connectivity.

8. **Simple Connection Process:** The user should only need to install MyAcs on both PCs, obtain the target PC's permanent ID, enter that ID on the viewing PC, and connect to view the screen.

9. **High-Quality Streaming:** Provide smooth, low-latency screen mirroring with adaptive resolution, efficient video encoding, and minimal CPU, memory, and network usage.

10. **Modern User Interface:** Design a clean, professional, modern interface with clear device IDs, connection status, available devices, connection controls, and a live screen-viewing window.

11. **Secure Connections:** Implement authentication, encrypted local network communication, and authorization so that only approved devices can view a PC's screen. Device IDs must not act as the sole security credential.

12. **Reliable Reconnection:** If the network temporarily disconnects or the target PC restarts, MyAcs should automatically restore availability and reconnect when possible.

### Expected Result

Build MyAcs as a fully functional Windows application, not a prototype or mockup. All device IDs, connections, screen streaming, background services, startup behavior, and reconnection mechanisms must work dynamically without hardcoded or dummy data.

The final application should allow me to view my own authorized PCs on the same local network at any time, even when the MyAcs application window is closed, provided the target PC is powered on and its background service is running.